{%- doc -%}
  Renders a single text node at one of ../design-system/src/react/Text/Text.tsx's roles and colour
  variants. Extracted from blocks/mionas-text.liquid so that block is not the only way to spend the
  role vocabulary: blocks/mionas-price.liquid renders its dynamic product copy through here instead
  of restating --text-role-* by hand, which is how it drifted out of step with the roles in the
  first place.

  The .text-role CSS lives in this snippet's stylesheet tag. Shopify ships only the stylesheet CSS
  of files a page renders, so the rules reach every page that renders this snippet, whichever
  block or section calls it.

  CALLERS MUST SANITISE `content` THEMSELVES. This snippet outputs it unfiltered, because
  mionas-text passes richtext that has already been flattened to inline HTML and the product blocks
  pass values from `| money` and product.title. Nothing here escapes; nothing here strips tags.

  @param {string} content - The text to render. Emitted unfiltered; see above.
  @param {string} [variant] - A Text.tsx variant: display, heading, subheading, title, lead, body, label. Defaults to body. `inherit` renders no variant, so size, line-height and tracking come from the surroundings.
  @param {string} [color] - A colour variant: default, primary, secondary, inverse-primary, inverse-primary-muted, accent, accent-inverse, tint. Defaults to default.
  @param {string} [transform] - uppercase, lowercase, capitalize or none. Unset leaves the inherited case.
  @param {string} [tag] - p, span, div, h1-h6, a or button. Anything else falls back to p.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes for the caller's own box (padding, weight overrides).
  @param {string} [style] - Inline declarations for the caller's own box. Emitted unfiltered like `content`, but unlike `content` it is NOT for caller HTML -- it exists so a block can pass its own inline CSS, such as snippets/spacing-style.liquid output (the --padding-* custom properties behind Horizon's `spacing-style` class) or a per-instance custom property the caller already validated the shape of (blocks/mionas-product-badges.liquid's per-badge accent colors, sourced from a Shopify `color`-type field so they are guaranteed "#rrggbb" or blank). Never pass merchant free text through here.
  @param {string} [attributes] - Raw extra attributes, such as a link's href. Caller-controlled only; never merchant free text.
  @param {string} [heading_level] - When set, emits role="heading" aria-level="<n>" instead of a real <h*>, matching snippets/text.liquid's product-title branch.
  @param {string} [shopify_attributes] - The caller's block.shopify_attributes, so the theme editor can still select the block.

  @example
  {% render 'mionas-text', content: product.title, variant: 'body', tag: 'p', class: 'mionas-price' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign resolved_variant = variant | default: 'body'
  assign resolved_color = color | default: 'default'

  comment
    A stale variant must fall back, not pass through: `default` only catches nil/blank, not a
    string that stopped being a valid variant, and an invalid class leaves the text with no size,
    weight or tracking at all. Keep this list in step with the .text-role--* rules below.
  endcomment
  assign allowed_variants = 'display|heading|subheading|title|lead|body|label' | split: '|'
  unless allowed_variants contains resolved_variant
    assign resolved_variant = 'body'
  endunless

  comment
    tag comes from a select in every caller today, but a snippet is reachable from anywhere, so an
    unknown value falls back to p rather than emitting an invalid element.
  endcomment
  assign allowed_tags = 'p|span|div|h1|h2|h3|h4|h5|h6|a|button' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_tag = tag | default: 'p'
  unless allowed_tags contains resolved_tag
    assign resolved_tag = 'p'
  endunless

  comment
    `inherit` is Link.tsx's opt-in: no variant class, so the element takes its size from its
    surroundings, and no colour class, so it takes their colour.
  endcomment
  assign classes = 'text-role'
  unless variant == 'inherit'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' text-role--' | append: resolved_variant
  endunless
  unless resolved_color == 'inherit'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' text-role--' | append: resolved_color
  endunless
  assign allowed_transforms = 'uppercase|lowercase|capitalize|none' | split: '|'
  if allowed_transforms contains transform
    assign classes = classes | append: ' text-role--transform-' | append: transform
  endif
  if class != blank
    assign classes = classes | append: ' ' | append: class
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Interpolated rather than switched through a {% case %}: resolved_tag is already whitelisted
  above, so a per-tag branch would have nothing left to guard.
{%- endcomment -%}
<{{ resolved_tag }}
  class="{{ classes }}"
  {%- if style != blank %}
    style="{{ style }}"
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if attributes != blank %}
    {{ attributes }}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if heading_level != blank %}
    role="heading"
    aria-level="{{ heading_level }}"
  {%- endif %}
  {{ shopify_attributes }}
>{{- content -}}</{{ resolved_tag }}>

{% stylesheet %}
  .text-role {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-family-archivo);
  }

  /* Keep the Variant select in blocks/mionas-text.liquid and the whitelist above in step with
     this list. */
  .text-role--display {
    font-size: var(--text-role-display-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-display-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-display-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-display-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--heading {
    font-size: var(--text-role-heading-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-heading-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-heading-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-heading-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--subheading {
    font-size: var(--text-role-subheading-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-subheading-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-subheading-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-subheading-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--title {
    font-size: var(--text-role-title-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-title-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-title-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-title-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--lead {
    font-size: var(--text-role-lead-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-lead-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-lead-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-lead-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--body {
    font-size: var(--text-role-body-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-body-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-body-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-body-letter-spacing);
  }

  .text-role--label {
    font-size: var(--text-role-label-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-label-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-label-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-label-letter-spacing);
  }

  /* No text-role--stamp rule here on purpose: snippets/mionas-stamp.liquid renders label and
     overrides its size there, mirroring Stamp.tsx's <Text variant="label">. */

  .text-role--default {
    color: var(--text-color-default);
  }

  .text-role--primary {
    color: var(--text-color-primary);
  }

  .text-role--secondary {
    color: var(--text-color-secondary);
  }

  .text-role--inverse-primary {
    color: var(--text-color-inverse-primary);
  }

  .text-role--inverse-primary-muted {
    color: var(--text-color-inverse-primary-muted);
  }

  .text-role--accent {
    color: var(--text-color-accent);
  }

  .text-role--accent-inverse {
    color: var(--text-color-accent-inverse);
  }

  .text-role--tint {
    color: var(--text-color-tint);
  }

  /* `none` exists so a text inside an uppercased container can opt back out. */
  .text-role--transform-uppercase {
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .text-role--transform-lowercase {
    text-transform: lowercase;
  }

  .text-role--transform-capitalize {
    text-transform: capitalize;
  }

  .text-role--transform-none {
    text-transform: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
